{"vulnerabilidade_identificada":"Race condition leading to inconsistent 'likedBy' updates allowing multiple likes from the same user.","causa_da_vulnerabilidade":"The code performs two separate database update operations: first incrementing 'likesCount' and then updating the 'likedBy' array after fetching the updated review. Between these operations, concurrent requests can interleave, causing the 'likedBy' array to be overwritten without proper synchronization, allowing a user to like the same review multiple times.","estrategia_de_correcao":"Combine the increment of 'likesCount' and the update of 'likedBy' array into a single atomic database update operation using MongoDB's $inc and $addToSet operators to prevent race conditions and ensure a user can only like once.","edicoes":[{"arquivo":"routes/likeProductReviews.ts","trecho_original":"      await db.reviewsCollection.update(
        { _id: id },
        { $inc: { likesCount: 1 } }
      )","trecho_corrigido":"      await db.reviewsCollection.update(
        { _id: id },
        { $inc: { likesCount: 1 }, $addToSet: { likedBy: user.data.email } }
      )"},{"arquivo":"routes/likeProductReviews.ts","trecho_original":"      // Artificial wait for timing attack challenge
      await sleep(150)
      try {
        const updatedReview: Review = await db.reviewsCollection.findOne({ _id: id })
        const updatedLikedBy = updatedReview.likedBy
        updatedLikedBy.push(user.data.email)

        const count = updatedLikedBy.filter(email => email === user.data.email).length
        challengeUtils.solveIf(challenges.timingAttackChallenge, () => count > 2)

        const result = await db.reviewsCollection.update(
          { _id: id },
          { $set: { likedBy: updatedLikedBy } }
        )
        res.json(result)
      } catch (err) {
        res.status(500).json(err)
      }","trecho_corrigido":"      // Artificial wait for timing attack challenge
      await sleep(150)
      try {
        const updatedReview: Review = await db.reviewsCollection.findOne({ _id: id })
        const updatedLikedBy = updatedReview.likedBy

        const count = updatedLikedBy.filter(email => email === user.data.email).length
        challengeUtils.solveIf(challenges.timingAttackChallenge, () => count > 2)

        res.json(updatedReview)
      } catch (err) {
        res.status(500).json(err)
      }"}],"justificativa_tecnica":"Using MongoDB's $addToSet operator atomically adds the user's email to the 'likedBy' array only if it does not already exist, preventing duplicates. Combining this with $inc in a single update operation eliminates the race condition caused by separate reads and writes, ensuring data consistency and that a user cannot like the same review multiple times.","limitacoes_da_correcao":"This fix assumes the database supports atomic update operators like $addToSet and $inc. The artificial sleep remains for the timing attack challenge and does not affect the fix. The solution does not prevent timing attacks but ensures data integrity regarding likes."}
